format: rslide/1
title: The warmest years on record
description: The eleven warmest years in NASA's record of 146 are the last eleven, 2015 to 2025.
version: 1.0.0
styles: [sleek]
---
title: The warmest years on record
subtitle: NASA's global temperature index, 1880 to 2025
---
metric:
  value: "1976"
  format: year
  label: The last year with a global temperature below the 1951–1980 average
source: NASA GISS GISTEMP v4, annual land–ocean temperature index
---
title: The index has risen since the late nineteenth century
subtitle: Annual global temperature anomaly, 1880 to 2025, against the 1951–1980 average
chart:
  type: line
  title: Global temperature has risen since the late nineteenth century
  data: { csv: data/global-temperature.csv }
  encoding: { x: year, y: anomaly_c }
  axes:
    x: { format: year }
    y: { label: Temperature anomaly, unit: °C }
source: NASA GISS GISTEMP v4, annual land–ocean temperature index
---
title: Since 1980 each twenty-year period is at least 0.3 °C warmer than the last
subtitle: Mean anomaly by twenty-year period; the last bar holds 2020 to 2025
left:
  - Weather moves single years: El Niño years stand above their neighbours, La Niña years below.
  - Twenty-year means smooth that out.
  - The forty years from 1940 to 1979 average zero.
right:
  chart:
    type: bar
    title: Mean anomaly by twenty-year period against the 1951–1980 average
    data:
      inline:
        - { period: "1880–99", mean: -0.22 }
        - { period: "1900–19", mean: -0.32 }
        - { period: "1920–39", mean: -0.18 }
        - { period: "1940–59", mean: 0.00 }
        - { period: "1960–79", mean: 0.00 }
        - { period: "1980–99", mean: 0.32 }
        - { period: "2000–19", mean: 0.70 }
        - { period: "2020–25", mean: 1.06 }
    encoding: { x: period, y: mean }
    axes:
      y: { label: "Mean anomaly, °C", min: -0.6, max: 1.4 }
cols: 9-15
source: NASA GISS GISTEMP v4, annual land–ocean temperature index; the means are worked out from its annual values
---
title: Every decade since the 1960s has been warmer than the one before
subtitle: Mean, coldest and warmest year of each decade, °C against 1951–1980
left:
  table:
    data:
      inline:
        - { decade: 1950s, mean: "−0.05", low: "−0.19", high: "0.08" }
        - { decade: 1960s, mean: "−0.03", low: "−0.20", high: "0.06" }
        - { decade: 1970s, mean: "0.04", low: "−0.10", high: "0.18" }
        - { decade: 1980s, mean: "0.25", low: "0.12", high: "0.39" }
        - { decade: 1990s, mean: "0.39", low: "0.22", high: "0.61" }
        - { decade: 2000s, mean: "0.59", low: "0.39", high: "0.68" }
        - { decade: 2010s, mean: "0.80", low: "0.61", high: "1.01" }
        - { decade: 2020–25, mean: "1.06", low: "0.85", high: "1.28" }
    columns:
      - { key: decade, label: Decade }
      - { key: mean, label: Mean, align: right }
      - { key: low, label: Coldest year, align: right }
      - { key: high, label: Warmest year, align: right }
right:
  - Since the 1980s even a decade's coldest year is above the baseline.
  - 2011, the coldest year of the 2010s, matched 1998, the warmest of the 1990s.
cols: 14-10
source: NASA GISS GISTEMP v4, annual land–ocean temperature index; the means are worked out from its annual values
---
title: The last eleven years
subtitle: 2015 to 2025
---
title: Every year since 2015 has been at least 0.85 °C above the average
subtitle: Annual anomaly against the 1951–1980 average, 2001 to 2025
top:
  chart:
    type: bar
    title: Annual global temperature anomaly, 2001 to 2025
    data:
      inline:
        - { year: "2001", anomaly: 0.53 }
        - { year: "2002", anomaly: 0.63 }
        - { year: "2003", anomaly: 0.62 }
        - { year: "2004", anomaly: 0.53 }
        - { year: "2005", anomaly: 0.68 }
        - { year: "2006", anomaly: 0.64 }
        - { year: "2007", anomaly: 0.66 }
        - { year: "2008", anomaly: 0.54 }
        - { year: "2009", anomaly: 0.66 }
        - { year: "2010", anomaly: 0.72 }
        - { year: "2011", anomaly: 0.61 }
        - { year: "2012", anomaly: 0.65 }
        - { year: "2013", anomaly: 0.67 }
        - { year: "2014", anomaly: 0.75 }
        - { year: "2015", anomaly: 0.89 }
        - { year: "2016", anomaly: 1.01 }
        - { year: "2017", anomaly: 0.91 }
        - { year: "2018", anomaly: 0.85 }
        - { year: "2019", anomaly: 0.98 }
        - { year: "2020", anomaly: 1.01 }
        - { year: "2021", anomaly: 0.85 }
        - { year: "2022", anomaly: 0.89 }
        - { year: "2023", anomaly: 1.17 }
        - { year: "2024", anomaly: 1.28 }
